    "created_at": "2016-06-27T16:45:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-27T16:45:53Z",
    "body": "FWIW, I don't know if it currently is, but I made the case on IRC that this should be case-sensitive. Otherwise we limit the namespace of a value defined by other standards. I think generally we should just go for case-sensitive where we can. HTML has been inconsistent on this thus far, case-insensitive only really makes sense for ASCII, and case-sensitive is just simpler to test and implement.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
